olid R. A Democratic-sponsored May poll showed a 53-47 race, but with no recent independent polling the forecast stays close to the fundamentals, landing slightly beyond the baseline given the ratings consensus and market pricing.", "watch": "A credible late-October independent poll showing Conroy within single digits, or a surge of Democratic outside spending, would signal the race tightening.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Michael Baumgartner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Michael Baumgartner seeks a second term against Democrat Carmela Conroy in a rematch of their 2024 contest. The Spokane-based district has a Republican lean of about five points, and no Democrat has carried it in three decades. Baumgartner has raised roughly $1.7 million and holds a wide cash advantage, while Conroy has raised about $396,000, with some Democratic outside money opposing the incumbent.\n\nMost expert raters place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, though a few call it Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Baumgartner roughly an 80 percent chance of winning. The only general-election polling is an older Democratic-sponsored survey showing a mid-single-digit race. The evidence points to a Republican win with modest but real uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0968, "margin": -8.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1087, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0951, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0945, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1116, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0732, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1005, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.124, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1258, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_de